def window_max(nums, k):
    if not nums or k <= 0:
        return []

    window = deque(nums[:k])
    maxes = []
    for i in range(k, len(nums)):
        max_in_window = max(window)
        while window and nums[i] > window[-1]:
            window.pop()
        window.append(nums[i])
        if i >= k - 1:
            maxes.append(max_in_window)
    return maxes
```

This function uses a deque (double-ended queue) to maintain the sliding window of size `k`. It iterates through the input list and for each element, it finds the maximum number in the current window and appends it to the `maxes` list if the window has been initialized (i.e., we have moved past the initial k elements). The time complexity is O(n) due to a single pass through the input list.

